1.1.1 Object Detection
Review:
Object localization: locate an object with a bounding box (a rectangle).
Image classification: identify the category (a text label) that an image belongs to.
Object detection: idetify both the location and category of objects in an image.

Suggested practice:

Use a photo app and some pictures to identify the objects in the pictures. Notice how taking photos at different angles,
or adjusting the bounding box can lead to different results for the suggested classes of the objects.

Apps used:

If you have a smartphone, your built-in photo app or photo album may have object detection built in. You can also download
Google Photos onto and Android or iPhone.

1.1.2 Similarity Search
Review:
Enbeddings are lists of numbers that describe an image in a compact way. Embeddings can be created for images, but also 
other things like text, audio.

The distance between two embeddings is measure of how similar the two images are.

Similarity search creates an embedding for the search image, and compares it to embeddings of other images in a database.
It identifies other images for which the embeddings are a shorter distance to the search image's embedding, and returns
those associated images as similar to the search image's embedding, and returns those associated images as similar to
the search image. This can be applied to other things like text and audio.

1.1.3 Image Segmentation

Rebiew:
Image segmentation identifies all the pixels that are associated with a particular object in an image.

