1.1.4 Optical Character Recognition

Review:
Optical Character Recognition extracts text from inside an image so that you can use the text in a word processor,
email or text message.

Apps used:
On a computer, in the Google Chrome web browser, you can use Google Lens on images shown inside the web browser.

Suggested practice:

Take a picture of a recepiet or document, and extract text from the image. Notice when it works well, and when it does
not. For instance, what if the text is arranged within a table?

